body:
Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: Query runtime; benefits from #215 plan advisor and workspace files.

## Goal
Let developers benchmark representative SQL before/after changes with reproducible context and compare latency/plan behavior.

## Scope
- define benchmark cases from saved/file queries;
- warmup count / measured runs;
- parameter sets;
- connection/environment binding;
- capture duration, rows, error, optional EXPLAIN metrics;
- before/after comparison across query versions or environments;
- median/p95/basic distribution summary;
- export benchmark report;
- history stored locally per workspace.

## Rules
- benchmarks are explicit, never automatic load tests;
- default concurrency = 1;
- production execution warns and can be policy-disabled;
- result rows bounded/discardable when only timing is needed;
- timings clearly distinguish client wall time from provider plan metrics.

## Acceptance
- benchmark suite runs deterministically enough to compare repeated local runs;
- cancellation stops remaining cases;
- comparison highlights regressions/improvements without overclaiming causality;
- parameter/value types remain canonical;
- service/runtime/native UI tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(query): add SQL benchmark suites and comparison`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: schema metadata cache; benefits from #273 snapshots and #199 compare.

## Goal
Detect when a connected database schema changes outside DB Pro and surface actionable drift without forcing users to discover it after stale errors.

## Scope
- lightweight periodic metadata fingerprint for active connections;
- configurable polling interval / manual-only mode;
- detect object additions/removals/changed signatures;
- notification with changed schemas/objects count;
- refresh metadata action;
- compare against workspace snapshot when available;
- invalidate completion/ER/object workbench caches safely;
- pause watcher for disconnected/inactive connections;
- per-connection enable/disable.

## Rules
- no aggressive catalog polling;
- watcher is metadata-only and readonly;
- production connections default to conservative interval;
- stale detection result versioned against connection/schema generation.

## Acceptance
- external table/column/index change is detected in fixture;
- completion/object tree refresh after acceptance;
- no continuous CPU/query churn while idle;
- switching connection rejects stale watcher results;
- service/runtime/native notification tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(schema): add background schema drift detection`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: canonical editor diagnostics/completion; benefits from #264/#268.

## Goal
Add lightweight contextual hints directly in SQL without cluttering the editor.

## Scope
CodeLens-style actions above statements:
- Run Current;
- Explain;
- Run in Sandbox;
- Open Referenced Table;
- Find References;
- Show Last Duration / Last Rows for executed statement.

Inlay hints:
- resolved schema for unqualified table;
- inferred parameter type;
- bound connection/database/schema context;
- ambiguous object warning hint;
- optional estimated row count/plan cost only after explicit explain metadata exists.

## Rules
- hints are configurable/off by default if too noisy;
- no hidden DB query per keystroke;
- provider metadata/cache only for passive resolution;
- performance must remain bounded for large SQL files.

## Acceptance
- hints update when connection/schema context changes;
- disabled settings remove them entirely;
- stale async results rejected by document version;
- clicking action dispatches canonical commands;
- editor/native UI tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(editor): add database-aware codelens and inlay hints`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #264 workspace index; related to #216 object dependencies and ER graph.

## Goal
Build a cross-domain dependency graph linking SQL files/migrations to live database objects so developers can understand blast radius before changes.

## Scope
Nodes:
- workspace SQL files;
- migration files;
- tables/views/materialized views;
- routines;
- types;
- indexes/constraints where useful.

Edges:
- file references object;
- object depends on object;
- migration creates/alters/drops object;
- query file uses object.

UX:
- graph and list/tree modes;
- incoming/outgoing dependencies;
- impact analysis for selected file/object;
- filter by edge type/root/schema;
- jump to exact file/range or object workbench;
- export impact report.

## Rules
- unresolved/ambiguous references visibly distinguished;
- graph generation is metadata/index based, no SQL execution;
- large graphs use existing scalable ER/spatial architecture where appropriate.

## Acceptance
- representative migration/query workspace produces correct mixed graph;
- impact analysis identifies dependent files/objects;
- cycles and unresolved refs handled;
- large project remains responsive;
- graph/index/native UI tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(ide): add workspace and database dependency graph`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261 workspace; related to #204 connection organization and #265 multi-root.

## Goal
Add workspace-level environment profiles so one project can switch coherently between Development, Staging, Production and custom targets without manually rebinding every SQL file/task.

## Scope
- named environments;
- bind connection/database/schema defaults;
- per-environment variables excluding secrets;
- root/file/task overrides;
- visible active-environment badge;
- quick switch command;
- environment-specific migration/test/task context;
- validation that referenced connection still exists;
- optional environment config file checked into workspace with connection IDs/aliases only.

## Safety
- secrets remain in secret store, never workspace files;
- Production visually distinct and strongly confirmed for destructive actions;
- switching environment never auto-runs queries/migrations;
- stale/missing connection binding blocks execution with clear error.

## Acceptance
- switching environment updates eligible file/task context consistently;
- explicit per-file override wins predictably;
- environment state restores per workspace;
- production safety policies remain enforced;
- service/native UI tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add environment profiles and context switching`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #272 migration project; benefits from #208 backup/restore and provider SDK.

## Goal
Provide a safe disposable environment for previewing migrations before touching a real target database.

## Scope
- create disposable SQLite copy or temporary PostgreSQL database/schema where supported;
- seed from schema snapshot or selected backup without production credentials leaking;
- apply pending migrations in sandbox;
- capture success/failure, schema diff and timing;
- preview resulting schema against intended target;
- tear down sandbox automatically/explicitly;
- retain logs/evidence optionally;
- allow Agent to reason over sandbox result, never auto-promote to production.

## Safety
- sandbox target must be visually distinct;
- no automatic production clone with row data;
- data copy is opt-in and bounded/masked where possible;
- sandbox credentials ephemeral;
- cleanup resilient to app restart.

## Acceptance
- PG/SQLite representative migration can be previewed end-to-end;
- failed migration reports exact step and leaves real DB untouched;
- resulting schema diff is inspectable;
- stale sandbox state cannot be mistaken for current target;
- service/provider/native UI tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(migrations): add disposable migration sandbox`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: Query runtime; benefits from #261 workspace and #270 task runner.

## Goal
Add a lightweight SQL regression-testing system for schema/data/query behavior inside database projects.

## Scope
- define SQL test files/suites in workspace;
- setup/fixture SQL;
- assertions such as row count, scalar equals, result snapshot, query succeeds/fails, schema object exists;
- per-test connection/environment binding;
- transactional isolation/rollback where provider supports it;
- run file/suite/all;
- test explorer/status/history;
- diff expected vs actual result;
- CI/headless runner later through same core service.

## Safety
- default tests target Development/Test contexts;
- production execution disabled by default;
- destructive fixtures require explicit test DB policy;
- assertions never rely on lossy string coercion for Decimal/BIGINT/time values.

## Acceptance
- representative PG/SQLite suites run deterministically;
- failing assertion shows actionable diff;
- rollback/isolation behavior explicit;
- test results map back to exact file/range;
- service/runtime/native UI tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(testing): add SQL regression test runner`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: Query runtime and workspace/file model.

## Goal
Add notebook-style database documents for exploratory analysis, incident notes, onboarding and reproducible investigations.

## Scope
- notebook file format with versioned schema;
- Markdown cells;
- SQL cells;
- per-cell connection/database/schema context;
- run cell / run above / run all;
- inline result grids/messages;
- collapse/expand cells;
- cell execution status/duration;
- clear outputs;
- export notebook to Markdown/HTML where practical;
- save under workspace and restore outputs optionally.

## Rules
- SQL execution uses canonical QueryService/safety pipeline;
- outputs are bounded and not silently embedded at unbounded size;
- production/destructive SQL keeps normal confirmation;
- notebook does not become a second SQL editor implementation.

## Acceptance
- mixed Markdown/SQL document round-trips losslessly;
- each SQL cell can bind explicit connection context;
- execution order/status is visible;
- restart preserves document structure;
- query/editor/notebook tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(ide): add SQL notebook documents`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: existing tab/query workspace; benefits from #262 file-backed SQL.

## Goal
Add IDE-grade split editor groups so users can compare/edit SQL, DDL, migration files and query results side-by-side.

## Scope
- split left/right and top/bottom;
- move tab between groups;
- duplicate view of same document without duplicating document state;
- independent cursor/selection/scroll per view;
- synchronized document edits;
- compare SQL vs generated DDL/migration;
- persist editor group layout in workspace session;
- close group / merge group / focus next group;
- keyboard commands for split/navigation.

## Rules
- QueryDocument remains canonical; editor views are projections;
- execution context stays document-bound unless explicitly overridden;
- duplicate view does not create duplicate draft/history state.

## Acceptance
- same SQL file can be viewed in two groups with shared text and independent view state;
- layout restores after restart;
- dirty/save semantics remain single-source;
- tab move/close cannot lose unsaved work;
- native UI/state tests.

Suggested commit: `feat(ide): add split editor groups and persistent layouts`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #264/#268; benefits from #199 compare and Phase A mutation framework.

## Goal
Add SQL-aware refactoring across workspace files, beginning with safe reference-aware rename planning.

## Scope
Initial refactors:
- rename table references across SQL workspace;
- rename column references where resolution is unambiguous;
- rename view/routine references;
- qualify/unqualify object references where safe;
- extract selected SQL to a new saved/file query as a non-semantic convenience refactor.

Rename flow:
1. resolve symbol/object;
2. find references;
3. classify exact/ambiguous/unresolved matches;
4. preview per-file diffs;
5. optionally include database object mutation when canonical mutation framework supports it;
6. explicit Apply.

## Safety
- never text-replace ambiguous identifiers blindly;
- strings/comments excluded unless explicitly intended;
- workspace edits and DB rename are separate reviewable operations;
- DB rename requires canonical mutation preview/confirmation;
- stale file versions block apply.

## Acceptance
- qualified and aliased references handled in representative fixtures;
- ambiguous references are not auto-edited;
- preview exactly matches writes;
- partial workspace-only rename supported;
- parser/index/refactor/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(editor): add SQL-aware workspace refactoring and rename`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261/#262/#263; benefits from #264 workspace index and existing Agent typed workflow.

## Goal
Let Agent propose coordinated edits across multiple SQL/migration files while preserving IDE-grade review, version checks, undo and database safety.

## Scope
Agent can propose:
- edit current SQL file;
- edit multiple selected SQL files;
- create a new migration file;
- update related query files;
- generate schema documentation artifacts.

Patch model must contain:
- target file;
- base version/hash;
- edits/new content;
- reason;
- optional DB object references.

Review UI:
- file tree of proposed changes;
- per-file diff;
- accept/reject file;
- accept/reject hunk if architecture supports;
- Apply Selected;
- conflict state when file changed since proposal;
- one-step workspace undo/recovery where feasible.

## Rules
- Agent never writes files before explicit approval;
- edits stay inside trusted workspace roots;
- secret/ignored files excluded by default;
- creating migration does not execute it;
- database mutations remain separate canonical actions with their own preview/confirmation;
- remote provider receives only disclosed selected context.

## Acceptance
- multi-file patch can be reviewed and partially applied;
- stale base hash blocks unsafe overwrite;
- rejected files remain unchanged;
- applied edits integrate with editor dirty/undo/file watcher state;
- migration generation creates file only, not DB mutation;
- Agent/service/native diff UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(agent): add reviewed multi-file SQL workspace edits`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261; benefits from #199 schema compare and Phase A object mutation framework.

## Goal
Allow a workspace to store versionable schema snapshots as files and compare/sync them with a live database, creating a bridge between IDE files, Git, migrations, and database metadata.

## Scope
- export canonical schema snapshot to workspace file;
- deterministic stable serialization suitable for Git diffs;
- open snapshot in structured viewer + raw representation;
- compare snapshot vs live schema;
- compare snapshot vs snapshot;
- generate migration plan from differences when #200 is available;
- link snapshot to connection/database/schema context without storing credentials;
- refresh snapshot explicitly;
- detect stale snapshot timestamp/fingerprint.

## Format
Use a versioned DB Pro schema representation (JSON/YAML or equivalent) containing canonical metadata, not provider-specific raw catalog rows.

## Safety
- snapshot may contain object definitions/comments but must not contain row data or credentials;
- sync-to-live always goes through mutation preview/safety;
- production apply remains strongly confirmed.

## Acceptance
- same unchanged schema produces stable diff-friendly output;
- snapshot/live compare identifies representative object changes;
- provider-specific metadata is normalized without pretending unsupported fields exist;
- Git can meaningfully review snapshot changes;
- service/serialization/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add versionable schema snapshots and live diff`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261/#262; related to #199/#200 compare/migration and #255 Git workspace.

## Goal
Treat migration folders as first-class IDE projects, connecting SQL files on disk to the actual database migration state.

## Scope
- detect/configure migration directories and naming conventions;
- migration tree ordered by version/timestamp;
- parse migration metadata where possible;
- status: Applied / Pending / Unknown / Diverged;
- configurable migration history table adapter rather than hardcoding one framework;
- compare workspace migrations against target database history;
- show current target connection/environment prominently;
- preview selected migration SQL;
- run pending migration through explicit configured runner/canonical SQL path;
- rollback only when project has explicit down migration/strategy;
- drift detection between expected schema snapshot/migrations and live DB where compare foundation exists.

## Framework adapters
Design for conventions such as Flyway/Liquibase/Prisma/Drizzle/SQLx/custom SQL without requiring all adapters in first implementation.

## Safety
- no automatic migration on folder open;
- production migration requires strong confirmation;
- exact files/versions to execute are previewed;
- history-table writes happen only through explicit migration execution flow.

## Acceptance
- ordered migration tree is deterministic;
- applied/pending status can be resolved for at least one configurable convention;
- duplicate/gap/divergence states are visible;
- execution records exact file/version and result;
- no migration runs against unintended connection context;
- service/native UI/runtime tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(migrations): add workspace migration project and drift status`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261; security foundation for #263 and #270.

## Goal
Add explicit workspace trust and secret-boundary semantics before local project files can influence Agent context or task execution.

## Scope
Workspace trust states:
- Untrusted
- Trusted
- Restricted.

For untrusted workspaces disable/gate:
- task execution;
- terminal task presets;
- Agent whole-folder context;
- automatic workspace configuration actions;
- external command hooks.

Secret detection/exclusion:
- `.env*`;
- PEM/private keys;
- common credential/config patterns;
- user-configurable sensitive globs;
- large binary/private artifacts.

UI:
- trust banner/status;
- manage trust;
- context picker marks excluded/sensitive files;
- explicit override for a selected file with disclosure.

## Rules
- opening a folder never executes code;
- trust is persisted by canonicalized workspace identity;
- moving/replacing workspace must not accidentally inherit trust incorrectly;
- detection is defensive, not a guarantee that no secret exists.

## Acceptance
- untrusted project cannot auto-run commands or bulk-send folder context;
- sensitive defaults are excluded deterministically;
- trust identity/path edge cases tested;
- Agent payload tests prove excluded files are absent;
- native UI clearly exposes current trust state.

Merge independently after W01, preferably before W03/W10 production enablement.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add trust and secret context boundaries`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261 workspace; related to #206/#213 database tasks.

## Goal
Add an integrated terminal/task surface so a DB project can run migration CLIs, scripts, tests and local tooling without leaving DB Pro.

## Scope
- terminal panel bound to workspace root;
- multiple terminal sessions;
- shell selection from platform defaults;
- cwd per workspace root;
- run configured workspace tasks;
- task definitions for commands such as migrations/tests/codegen;
- task output, exit status, duration and history;
- clickable file references when parseable;
- cancel/terminate process;
- environment variable allowlist/override configuration.

## Security
- never expose DB Pro secret-store values to terminal automatically;
- no Agent command execution without explicit approval;
- workspace task command is displayed before first execution or when changed;
- untrusted workspace config cannot silently auto-run tasks;
- production DB credentials are not injected implicitly.

## Architecture
Terminal/process execution must live behind a process/task service, not renderer shell calls.

## Acceptance
- shell opens in correct workspace root;
- task execution streams output without blocking UI;
- cancellation cleans child process tree where platform allows;
- unsafe/untrusted task config requires explicit trust;
- cross-platform service/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(ide): add integrated terminal and workspace task runner`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261; benefits from #257 SQL linting and #264 workspace index.

## Goal
Create an IDE-style Problems surface aggregating diagnostics across open and indexed SQL files.

## Scope
Aggregate:
- parser diagnostics;
- SQL lint findings;
- unresolved/ambiguous object references;
- migration ordering/duplicate-version problems;
- provider validation errors when explicitly run;
- stale file/context conflicts.

UI:
- severity counts;
- filter by workspace root/file/source;
- group by file;
- click -> exact line/range;
- quick fix action when canonical fix exists;
- next/previous problem keyboard commands.

## Architecture
Use versioned diagnostics keyed by file/version so stale async results cannot overwrite newer edits.

## Rules
- offline/static findings distinguished from provider/runtime validation;
- no background execution of arbitrary SQL merely to produce diagnostics;
- provider validation must be explicit and readonly-safe.

## Acceptance
- diagnostics update after edit without stale flicker;
- Problems panel remains responsive for large workspaces;
- navigation targets exact range;
- severity/source filters deterministic;
- diagnostics/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(ide): add workspace SQL problems panel`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #264 workspace index; benefits from canonical database metadata.
Related: #216 object dependency navigator.

## Goal
Provide code-navigation semantics across SQL files and live database metadata.

## Scope
From SQL editor:
- Go to Definition for workspace-defined views/functions/CTEs where resolvable;
- Open Database Object for referenced table/view/routine;
- Find References across workspace SQL files;
- document symbols / outline;
- workspace symbol search;
- hover/basic metadata summary for resolved DB objects;
- Peek Definition-style compact preview where native UI supports it;
- breadcrumb symbol context.

Resolution rules must handle:
- qualified vs unqualified names;
- current connection/database/schema/search path context;
- aliases;
- ambiguous names;
- unresolved references.

## Rules
- best-effort resolution must never pretend ambiguity is certainty;
- database lookup uses metadata cache/services, not provider calls from editor renderer;
- navigation does not execute SQL.

## Acceptance
- table reference can jump to DB object or workspace definition as appropriate;
- references return exact file/range;
- ambiguity has explicit chooser/status;
- symbol extraction updates incrementally;
- parser/index/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(editor): add SQL definitions references and symbol navigation`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #264 workspace index.
Related: #201 global search.

## Goal
Add IDE-grade workspace text search and safe multi-file replacement, with SQL-aware filters.

## Scope
- Find in Files;
- regex / case / whole-word toggles;
- include/exclude glob patterns;
- result grouping by file;
- preview snippets and exact ranges;
- jump to result;
- Replace one / Replace all;
- replacement preview before applying multi-file changes;
- undo/recovery strategy for batch replacement;
- SQL-aware filters such as statement kind or referenced object where index data exists.

## Performance
- use workspace index where possible;
- stream/paginate large result sets;
- cancellation;
- incremental refresh after edits.

## Safety
- ignored/secret paths remain excluded unless explicitly overridden;
- replacement never touches binary/unsupported files;
- externally changed files are conflict-checked before write;
- batch replacement displays affected file count and diff preview.

## Acceptance
- thousands-file workspace remains responsive;
- regex and glob filters deterministic;
- replace-all can be reviewed before disk mutation;
- stale file conflicts prevent unsafe overwrite;
- search/index/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add find and replace across SQL projects`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261, #262.

## Goal
Make workspace navigation feel like a real IDE rather than a read-only file picker.

## Scope
File tree actions:
- New File / New Folder;
- Rename;
- Delete with confirmation;
- Duplicate;
- Reveal in system file manager;
- Copy absolute/relative path;
- refresh subtree.

Editor/navigation:
- breadcrumbs;
- back/forward navigation;
- recently opened files;
- tab pinning;
- preview tab semantics for single-click vs permanent open;
- close others / close right / reopen closed;
- dirty-file protection;
- Save All;
- file/folder context menus.

## Safety
- never delete dirty/open files without confirmation;
- detect external modification before rename/delete/save;
- filesystem actions restricted to selected workspace roots;
- symlink escapes handled explicitly.

## Acceptance
- file operations reconcile tree and open tabs immediately;
- navigation history jumps to exact file/range when known;
- dirty state cannot be silently lost;
- keyboard navigation works without mouse;
- filesystem/native UI tests.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add IDE file operations and navigation history`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261.

## Goal
Evolve the single-folder workspace into an IDE-grade multi-root workspace so one DB Pro window can combine application SQL, migrations, analytics queries, and generated schema artifacts from multiple roots.

## Scope
- Add/remove/reorder workspace roots;
- persist named workspace configuration;
- root-specific ignore/include rules;
- root-specific default connection/database/schema context;
- root badges and compact tree presentation;
- workspace config file (`dbpro.workspace.json` or equivalent) with versioned schema;
- Open Workspace / Save Workspace As;
- migration path and SQL folder conventions per root;
- safe path canonicalization and duplicate-root detection.

## Rules
- connection references use IDs, never credentials;
- no implicit production execution from workspace config;
- workspace config is portable where possible and can contain relative paths;
- missing roots remain visible with recovery UX instead of silently disappearing.

## Acceptance
- multiple roots render and restore correctly;
- root-specific context binding works;
- duplicate/nested root edge cases are deterministic;
- config migrations are tested;
- large roots do not block UI.

Merge independently.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add multi-root workspace configuration`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261 workspace folders.
Related: #201 global search, #263 context picker, #257 SQL linting.

## Goal
Index an opened workspace so DB Pro can search and reason across SQL files like an IDE instead of treating the folder tree as passive storage.

## Scope
Workspace index should cover supported text files with emphasis on SQL/migration assets.

Capabilities:
- filename/path search;
- full-text search;
- SQL statement inventory per file;
- best-effort table/view/routine references extracted from parseable SQL;
- migration-file ordering metadata where conventions are detectable/configured;
- references from SQL file -> database objects;
- reverse lookup: object -> workspace SQL files that reference it;
- search results jump to file/line/range;
- incremental index update on file changes;
- ignore rules inherited from W01.

## SQL project intelligence
For parseable SQL files expose lightweight symbols such as:
- statements;
- CTE names;
- table aliases;
- referenced tables/views;
- CREATE/ALTER/DROP target objects;
- routine definitions where parser supports them.

This is not a full SQL language server requirement initially.

## Search integration
Global Search should eventually query both:
- live database metadata;
- workspace index.

Results must clearly distinguish:
`DB Object` vs `Workspace File/Symbol`.

## Agent/context integration
W03 folder/file context should use this index for relevance and bounded retrieval instead of reading every workspace file blindly.

## Performance
- index work runs off UI thread;
- incremental updates rather than full rescan on every edit;
- cancellation/versioning for workspace switch;
- large repositories remain bounded;
- binary/generated/ignored files excluded.

## Safety/privacy
- index remains local by default;
- index content is not automatically sent to AI;
- secret-like files excluded according to workspace policy.

## Acceptance
- workspace with thousands of files can be indexed without freezing native UI;
- edits update relevant search results incrementally;
- search result opens exact file/range;
- referenced DB objects are resolved when metadata exists and remain unresolved-but-visible otherwise;
- workspace switch rejects stale indexing results;
- context picker can retrieve relevant SQL files/snippets through the index;
- service/parser/native UI tests.

Merge independently after W01.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add SQL project indexing and search intelligence`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261 workspace folders; benefits from #201 global search and existing Agent context system.

## Goal
Add a unified context-selection model so users can explicitly choose what DB Pro/Agent should reason over: workspace folders/files, current SQL selection, query tab, table/schema objects, query results, and database metadata.

## UX
Provide a context picker similar to modern coding IDE/AI workflows.

Examples:
- Add current SQL selection
- Add current file
- Add folder `migrations/`
- Add table `public.orders`
- Add schema `public`
- Add query result sample
- Add ER neighborhood
- Add diagnostics/error

Selected context appears as removable chips/items before sending an Agent request.

## Context model
Suggested canonical types:
- `WorkspaceFileContext`
- `WorkspaceFolderContext`
- `SqlSelectionContext`
- `QueryDocumentContext`
- `SchemaObjectContext`
- `SchemaContext`
- `QueryResultContext`
- `DiagnosticContext`
- `ErNeighborhoodContext`.

Each item carries:
- stable identity;
- display label;
- source/version/fingerprint;
- estimated size/token cost;
- sensitivity classification;
- refresh/stale state.

## Folder context
Folder selection must not blindly concatenate every file.

Pipeline:
folder
-> bounded file discovery
-> supported file filtering
-> search/index relevance
-> selected snippets/files
-> explicit context summary.

Provide include/exclude patterns and size limits.

## SQL context
Support:
- current selection;
- current statement;
- whole current SQL file/document;
- multiple explicitly selected SQL files.

Selection takes precedence when user explicitly selects text.

## Database context
Allow explicit objects:
- connection metadata excluding secrets;
- schema;
- table/view;
- columns/indexes/FKs;
- routine source;
- query result sample.

Reuse canonical schema metadata and Agent sampling limits.

## Safety/privacy
- `.env`, keys, credential files and ignored secret paths excluded by default;
- show exactly which context items will leave the machine when using remote AI;
- large folders/results require bounded sampling/indexing;
- context can be removed before send;
- never silently add whole database row data;
- stale file/schema context must be refreshed or visibly marked stale.

## Acceptance
- user can combine file + SQL selection + table metadata in one Agent request;
- folder context stays bounded on large repositories;
- secret/ignored files are excluded by default;
- context chip removal changes actual payload;
- version/fingerprint prevents silently using stale SQL/file contents;
- remote-AI disclosure lists context categories being sent;
- unit/service/native UI/Agent payload tests.

Merge independently after W01 foundation; W02 improves SQL-file integration but is not required for schema-only contexts.
Suggested commit: `feat(agent): add unified workspace and database context picker`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #261 workspace tree.
Related: #211 Queries Activity, #255 Git-backed workspace.

## Goal
Make `.sql` files inside an opened workspace first-class QueryDocuments so DB Pro behaves like an IDE: click a SQL file in the tree, edit it in the canonical SQL editor, run selections/statements, save it, and preserve its connection context.

## Scope
- open `.sql` from workspace tree in existing Query Editor;
- one canonical file-backed QueryDocument, not a second editor model;
- dirty indicator and save/save-all;
- external file-change detection with reload/compare prompt;
- file path/breadcrumb in editor header;
- per-file preferred connection/database/schema context;
- Run Current / Selection / All on file-backed document;
- history entries reference file path + execution context;
- reopen file-backed tabs on workspace restore;
- duplicate/open same file resolves to one document unless explicit split-view support is added later.

## Project SQL conventions
Allow optional workspace metadata to map folders/files to connection contexts, for example:
- `queries/analytics/*.sql` -> analytics connection;
- `migrations/*.sql` -> development/staging by explicit mapping.

No automatic production execution based only on folder name.

## Architecture
File backing belongs to QueryDocument persistence/lifecycle, while execution still goes through the canonical Query runtime.

Suggested additions:
- `QueryDocumentSource::{Scratch,Saved,File}`;
- `WorkspaceFileRef`;
- file version/hash for stale-write detection;
- context binding separate from SQL text.

## Safety
- never overwrite externally modified SQL silently;
- workspace file path cannot bypass normal readonly/destructive execution safety;
- saved connection context stores IDs/references, never credentials;
- production context remains visibly identified and confirmation-gated.

## Acceptance
- click SQL file -> canonical editor tab;
- edit/save/restart round-trip is lossless;
- external modifications are detected before overwrite;
- execution uses selected/bound connection without changing file contents;
- unsaved SQL survives tab switching according to existing draft policy;
- undo/redo/completion/diagnostics behave the same as scratch QueryDocuments;
- native UI + persistence/runtime tests.

Merge independently after W01.
Suggested commit: `feat(workspace): add file-backed SQL query documents`

